        "date": "2026-11-12T10:21:43Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): read a lathe holder body on the holder's own side of the axis\n\nThe holder law (#369) read a body point at |X + x| with X signed along\nthe path's meridian, whose + side is the path's first off-axis point.\nA rear tool starting a hair past centre put every later tip at X < 0 of\nthat frame, and its body was read mirrored through the axis - a lip\nreaching the part judged clear. The holder's side is now a per-path\nproperty (the side the path reaches farthest on, a past-centre overrun\nof at most 2.5 mm allowed on the other); the body is read at -X on the\n- side, and the drawn body flips its radial alike. A path on both sides\nbeyond that is refused by name. Generated paths (every tip at rho >= 0)\nread byte-identically to before.\n\nFixes #1102\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
